{
	title: 'Messages carry their sender; the send tool',
	description: "A message says who sent it: the user, or another session. The host sets the sender from the sending session, never from what a client claims. The model sees a session's message prefixed with who sent it (tab, id and name, like the old Hal's '[Inbox · <id>]' line) and every client shows the sender on the message, so nobody mistakes an agent for the user. The user's messages steer by default (task 2r). A `send` tool (one file under src/host/tools/) lets a session message another by tab number or id: advisory by default, `steer: true` to steer as the user would, `queue: true` to run it after the target's current turn. An advisory message is delivered as soon as possible, at the same point as steering (with the next tool results, or right after a round that had none), framed so the recipient reads it now but needn't drop its work for it; an idle recipient gets it as a turn of its own and gives it full attention. Sending to itself or to an unknown session is an error result. Up never recalls a message from another session (task dg). Artifacts: old-send.ts (the old tool), old-api-messages-excerpt.ts (how the old Hal framed inbox messages).",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Sender = { from?, label?, advisory? } (common/blocks.ts) sits on inbox records, InboxItem and each text block of a user record (UserText); `label` ('tab 2 · 156-eds · name') is fixed when sent, so replay stays byte-identical for the prompt cache. Events: turn-start.sender, prompt.senders (parallel to texts, only when some text is another session's); transcript prompt Items carry from and label, and both clients show '(sent from <label>)' like commands.",
		"replay.framed puts '[Inbox · <label>]' above another session's text and, if advisory, replay.advisoryNote below it. Advisory is dropped whenever the message runs as a turn of its own (idle submit, drain, queue), so it only frames mid-turn deliveries.",
		"The protocol's submit no longer has `from`: only the host (send tool calling prompts.submit with a Sender) marks a sender; a client's `from` is ignored. Tests that need another session's message call prompts.submit directly.",
		"Decision: a message from another session to a paused, failed or blocked session waits in the inbox (like a queued one) instead of starting a turn, so an agent never undoes the user's pause; continue delivers it.",
		"ToolContext now has sessionId (the calling session). prompts.amend edits the human's last text in the last prompt, keeping others' texts and their senders; a prompt with no human text makes the edit go on top."
	],
	needs: ['gr', 'dg', '2r']
}
